# ClawHub publish exclusions
# Keep these in the GitHub repo, but drop them from the published skill bundle.
# Principle: the published bundle = runtime body only (SKILL.md + engine + references/templates/docs).
# Repo governance, dev/test artifacts, and the license file stay in Git but never ship in the package.

# --- test & dev artifacts (never part of the runtime) ---
scripts/tests/
scripts/__pycache__/
scripts/.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- repo governance / contributor docs (not the skill runtime) ---
.github/
.gitignore
LICENSE
CHANGELOG.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
STATUS.md
README.md
README_EN.md

# --- python project metadata (ClawHub doesn't pip-install; engine only needs `python` on PATH) ---
pyproject.toml
